; GrassCommonShort — Grass terrain dressing (open_grass). Source: Stylized Nature MegaKit
; (Standard/free), Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — see
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres. Same source mesh
; (Grass_Common_Short.gltf) as every earlier pass; nothing new was sourced for this rework.
;
; MULTIMESH REWORK (2026-08-16, human-reported): explicit human complaint — "grass and
; wild grass... still spotty. I think they could stand to be shorter height, and more
; instances (30+)." The prior version hand-placed 10 individual MeshInstance3D nodes (one
; scene-tree node per blade cluster); getting to 30+ the same way would mean 30+ real
; nodes PER TILE, which terrain_view.gd's own header flags as "a known cost at the ~128x128
; cap, not at the ~36x36 start" — adding that many full nodes per grass tile pushes toward
; that cost much sooner than the mist-growth cap intends.
;
; Rebuilt instead around a SINGLE MultiMeshInstance3D ("GrassMultiMesh" below): one
; MultiMesh resource referencing the same Grass_Common_Short mesh, holding 36 BAKED
; Transform3D instances (position + Y-rotation + mild scale jitter — same repetition-plus-
; variation idiom as the hand-placed version, just data instead of nodes). 36 clears the
; human's "30+" floor with headroom. Generated by a deterministic, fixed-seed scatter
; (seed 20260816) within +/-0.42 tile-units of tile center (stays inside the new 1.0 slab
; without clipping into a neighboring tile — see the seam-gap fix note below) — one build
; pass, not randomized per tile at runtime; every GrassCommonShort tile in the game shows
; the identical baked pattern, same as every other terrain variant in this codebase.
;
; HEIGHT REDUCED: scale baseline dropped from the prior 0.112 (~0.15 tile-units tall) to
; 0.075 (~0.10 tile-units tall, +/-18% jitter) — a real, visible shortening, aimed at a
; "lawn" read instead of "tall isolated blades" per the human's wording. FLAG FOR HUMAN
; SIGN-OFF: 0.075 is a first-pass proposal, no GDD number exists for grass height (same
; posture as every prior scale call in this file's history).
;
; MESH EMBEDDED, NOT ExtResource-REFERENCED: MultiMesh.mesh needs a real Mesh resource,
; and the imported Grass_Common_Short.gltf only exposes a PackedScene (its mesh is not a
; separately addressable resource file — `materials/extract` was never enabled at import).
; The mesh was pulled out of the imported PackedScene at build time and is now embedded
; directly as an ArrayMesh sub_resource in this file — a deliberate, documented technical
; choice, not an oversight. It is still the exact same CC0 Quaternius geometry; sourcing/
; attribution is unchanged (see quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres).
;
; BUILT VIA A ONE-OFF HEADLESS SCRIPT, NOT HAND-TRANSCRIBED: MultiMesh's per-instance
; transform buffer is a flat PackedFloat32Array in a specific 12-floats-per-instance
; layout; hand-writing that risks silent, hard-to-catch errors (skewed/misplaced
; instances). Built instead by a throwaway Godot script (run via
; `godot --headless --script`, then deleted) using Godot's own Transform3D/MultiMesh/
; ResourceSaver APIs — the engine computed the actual serialized values, not a manual
; guess. One real wrinkle: under `--headless`, Godot's dummy RenderingServer backend does
; not implement `MultiMesh.set_instance_transform()`/`get_instance_transform()` (both
; silently no-op / read back identity) — confirmed by a standalone probe before writing
; the build tool. Worked around by writing the documented row-major buffer layout directly
; to the `buffer` property (a plain Resource property, unaffected by the RenderingServer
; gap), which DOES round-trip correctly through save/load.
;
; EVERYTHING NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" (kept from this codebase's established
; OcclusionFader-exemption convention — see CommonTree1.tscn's header for the full
; mechanism): a grass tile can sit as the "old" visual for one transient frame under a
; freshly-forested tile (TerrainView's queue_free() on the old visual is deferred, not
; immediate), so its ground box and multimesh both live under a wrapper Node3D literally
; named "Slab", exactly like WildGrass.tscn and both CommonTree scenes already do.
;
; SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0 (2026-08-16, human-reported cross-tile seam gap, same pass but a
; separate complaint from the density one above): `WorldGrid.TILE_SIZE` is 1.0, so a 0.94
; slab left a real 0.03-unit gap on every tile edge showing the sky-blue WorldEnvironment
; background straight through between adjacent tiles — the opposite of the intended read.
; Widened X/Z to exactly 1.0 (an exact TILE_SIZE match; 1.0 is exactly representable in
; float, so adjacent tile edges meet with no accumulation error). Y (0.2) untouched. Same
; fix applied identically across all terrain scenes this pass touches — see
; content-pipeline-status.md -> Terrain.
